# robonix/skill/p2pmov/move — navigate to a point.
#
# Provide EITHER a named point (`point_name`, resolved from the deployment
# config `points` dict) OR a raw goal coordinate (`x`, `y`, `yaw`).
# `point_name` wins when both are present.
#
# The goal is dispatched via the vendor TBox SDK task_distribution(); the
# chassis navigates autonomously on its onboard vendor map. Returns
# immediately with a run_id — poll move/status with that run_id to track
# arrival; abort with move/cancel.
string point_name   # key into config points dict; "" = use x/y/yaw
float64 x           # goal X in the onboard map frame (metres)
float64 y           # goal Y in the onboard map frame (metres)
float64 yaw         # goal heading, passed through verbatim (vendor unit)
---
bool accepted       # false if not authorized / unknown point / dispatch error
string run_id       # task handle; pass to move/status and move/cancel
string message      # human-readable detail (resolved target / error)
